1
00:00:00,574 --> 00:00:04,414
(Leonard:)But we don't need to quibble
over terminology.

2
00:00:04,578 --> 00:00:06,458
(Lesley:)What sort of experiment
would you propose?

3
00:00:06,622 --> 00:00:09,162
(Leonard:)There is a generally accepted
pattern in this area.

4
00:00:09,333 --> 00:00:12,583
I pick you up, take you to a restaurant,
then we would see a movie.

5
00:00:12,753 --> 00:00:15,093
(Leonard:)Probably a romantic comedy
featuring the talents...

6
00:00:15,255 --> 00:00:17,345
(Leonard:)...of Hugh Grant or Sandra Bullock.

7
00:00:17,966 --> 00:00:19,006
(Lesley:)Interesting.

8
00:00:19,176 --> 00:00:21,766
(Lesley:)And would you agree
the primary way we would evaluate...

9
00:00:21,929 --> 00:00:25,809
(Lesley:)...the success or failure of the date would
be based on the biochemical reaction...

10
00:00:25,974 --> 00:00:29,394
- ...during the good-night kiss?
- Heart rate, pheromones, et cetera, yes.

11
00:00:30,020 --> 00:00:32,020
Why don't we stipulate
the date goes well...

12
00:00:32,189 --> 00:00:33,979
...and move to the key variable?

13
00:00:34,149 --> 00:00:35,859
- You mean kiss you now?
- Yes.

14
00:00:36,026 --> 00:00:39,116
(Leonard:)- Define the parameters of the kiss.
- Closed mouth, but romantic.

15
00:00:39,279 --> 00:00:41,029
(Lesley:)- Mint?
- Thank you.

16
00:00:45,327 --> 00:00:46,577
[MINTS CRACKING]

17
00:00:48,163 --> 00:00:59,023
(Leonard:)- Shall I count down from three?
- No, I think it needs to be spontaneous.

